                <pb facs="0159" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg57"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.5221/15</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Riaño</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April 21,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5–02</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: By order of His Majesty’s
                    Government, I have the honor to apply to Your Excellency and to say that the
                    Ambassador of the United States at Madrid sent under date of the 11th instant a
                    note in which he puts on the extension of the Treaty of Friendship and General
                    Relations the condition that all discriminations in regard to customs and coal
                    shipments from Europe and America will be discontinued in Spain and that the
                    claims preferred by the Embassy against the Income Tax Law will cease, and that
                    the matter is to be taken under advisement and given urgent attention, but as
                    the Treaty expires on the 8th of May next, it directs me to apply to Your
                    Excellency in order to have the Government of the United States kindly grant an
                    extension of time of two months in which the proposition can be duly examined by
                    the Spanish official departments concerned, it being understood that Articles 23
                    and 24 will immediately be excluded.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
